From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Input: himax-spi: let the IC idle while nothing touches the panel

With the screen on the IC scans at 120 Hz and the driver reads and
processes every 5 KB frame whether or not anything touches the panel:
120 touch and 120 SPI interrupts a second and about 1.3 % of a CPU.
Unbinding the driver on a still screen saved 0.33-0.4 W of 5.4 W.

The firmware has an IDLE scan.  Asked through its command mailbox (five
16-byte slots at 0x10007550, written the way the vendor's Windows driver
writes them), it sends a frame only every three seconds or so, says so
in status word 0, and wakes up by itself when a finger or the pen comes.
After idle_ms (default 3000, <= 0 = never) of frames without a zone, a
track or the firmware's finger flag, send enter-IDLE, up to 8 times
100 ms apart.  If the IC still scans a second after the last one, or
wakes up again with nothing on the panel, wait idle_ms again and ask
again.  Times, not frame counts, so this holds at any scan rate.  The
mailbox and its write pointer are cleared at every init, as the Windows
driver does.  IDLE frames go through the pipeline as usual: their raw
grid stays within the noise of a normal empty frame (154 at most apart,
baseline_gate is 305).

The cascade slave slows down in IDLE as well.  himax-cascade.h shares
two things with its driver.  Whether the IC is idle, while its frames
say so and from the first enter-IDLE until a touch, a wake-up or a new
wait: the slave then sends a frame every three seconds or so too, so the
pen driver neither counts reads without a new frame as bad nor lets its
watchdog re-init the slave, as long as a frame with the 5a a5 header
came within 10 s (a slave that a master reset took down sends none).
And when the pen was last in use (a frame with the pen in it, or
userspace's hint that the pen controller is reporting): the pen leaves
no trace in the master's frames, so for 3 s after pen use frames do not
count as quiet (IDLE is requested idle_ms after that), as in the
vendor's software.  An IC already in IDLE is not forced out: it wakes up
when it notices the pen, and the vendor's software does not force it out
either.  The pen driver now depends on the touchscreen driver.

The stats attribute gains idle_cmds, idle_frames, ic_idle and
idle_state.

